# Physioguide — dual sync (código + conocimientos)

When implementing or updating a Physioguide clinical module, **always do BOTH**:

## 1. Code (deterministic — always applied)

- `knowledge/clinical-reasoning/<module>.md` — full clinical module
- `lib/physioguide-<module>-rules.ts` — AI rules constant
- Wire into `lib/ai-consult-rules.ts`, `mobile/src/lib/ai-consult-rules.ts`, `supabase/functions/ai-consult/response-rules.ts`
- Expand adaptive questionnaire + `lib/clinical-reasoning/trees.ts` (+ mobile copies)
- Deploy `ai-consult` edge function after rule changes
- Append hip/region rules to **physio_chat** and **physio_report** prompts in `supabase/functions/ai-consult/index.ts` when the module is region-specific

## 2. Conocimientos RAG (retrieved + citable)

After code is ready, ingest the markdown module:

```bash
node scripts/ingest-clinical-reasoning.mjs
```

Or one file: `node scripts/ingest-clinical-reasoning.mjs hip-lateral-pain.md`

Source titles use prefix `Physioguide — …` so RAG and Admin list them clearly.

## 3. Fase 3 evidence DB (tests + clusters)

When adding structured test/cluster evidence (not a clinical region module):

- `knowledge/evidence/<file>.md` — formato master §21 (Purpose…AI rule + Citation)
- `lib/physioguide-evidence-db-rules.ts` (+ mobile) if rules change
- Ingest: `node scripts/ingest-clinical-reasoning.mjs hip-tests.md`
- Prefix: `Physioguide — Evidencia — …`
- Never invent Sn/Sp; mark mixed evidence explicitly

## Who uses what

| Surface | Hardcoded rules | RAG (document_chunks) |
|---------|-----------------|------------------------|
| Consulta paciente | Yes (AI_EVIDENCE…) | Yes (fetchRagContext) |
| Fisioterapia tab (informe) | Yes (physio_report + rules) | Yes |
| /fisio/consulta Physio chat | Yes (physio_chat + rules) | Yes |

Both paths must stay aligned. Never ship code-only Physioguide modules without running the ingest script.
